Since the act.svg already works without any special install steps (except
for some non-critical optional npm package features), a command line could
be given for bash (on linux) to launch it.

ns-clone act git@github.com:koreyhinton/act.svg.git

It could have an 'svg' bash file, and with the 'act' prefix, it could be
launched from the command line, launching a web interface (maybe just the
default browser).

act-svg  # normal launch

# Other launch actions (e.g., test runner, version printer):

act_action="version"
act-svg  # prints the version

act_action="test"
act-svg  # runs tests

